<% content_for :title, "About | Corruption Tracker" %>

<article class="about-page" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
  <header class="about-page__header">
    <p class="home-eyebrow">About this project</p>
    <h1 id="about-heading">A clearer way to follow the Madlanga Commission</h1>
    <p class="about-page__introduction">
      Corruption Tracker is a helper app for anyone interested in following the Madlanga Commission and understanding what is emerging from its hearings.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-page__content">
    <section>
      <h2>Following the connections</h2>
      <p>
        The hearings introduce many people, organisations, events and allegations. This app maps the relationships that emerge from testimony so that you can follow those connections and learn more about what witnesses are saying.
      </p>
      <p>
        All information presented here is drawn directly from the Commission’s publicly accessible hearing transcripts. The aim is to make that public record easier to explore, not to replace the transcripts or the Commission’s own findings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How AI was used</h2>
      <p>
        AI helped extract information from the transcripts and explain the relationships between records. That work can be imperfect, and the site will evolve as more testimony and evidence become available.
      </p>
      <p>
        If something needs correcting, or if there is stronger evidence or context that warrants a change, please share it. Thoughtful feedback is warmly welcomed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <aside class="about-page__note">
      <p class="home-eyebrow">A labour of love</p>
      <p>
        I have spent the past year bringing this project to life because I believe the public should be able to follow these stories and connections more easily. I am excited to keep improving it—and to see where it goes from here.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</article>
